    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nMiniBufremove\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nnVim crashes when trying to wipeout a particular type of a buffer.\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\nNVIM v0.10.2 Build type: Release LuaJIT 2.1.1713484068\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. Install Ansible language server and `lspconfig.ansiblels.setup({})`\r\n2. Execute `<S-k>` on any keyword\r\n3. Observe documentation opened in a split\r\n4. **important** move mouse cursor from pseudo command-line to anywhere in the buffer\r\n4. Execute `MiniBufremove.wipeout()`\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nBuffer is closed, split is closed.\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\n```\r\nE315: ml_get: Invalid lnum: 1\r\nError detected while processing CursorMoved Autocommands for \"*\":\r\nE16: Invalid range: call s:Highlight_Matching_Pair()\r\nError detected while processing WinScrolled Autocommands for \"*\":\r\nE16: Invalid range: call s:Highlight_Matching_Pair()\r\nError detected while processing SafeState Autocommands for \"*\":\r\nE16: Invalid range: call s:Highlight_Matching_Pair()\r\nE315: ml_get: Invalid lnum: 1\r\nError detected while processing function <SNR>67_RunDeferred: line    5:\r\nE16: Invalid range:   call timer_start(0, function('s:RunDeferred'))\r\nE16: Invalid range:   call call(Fn, [])\r\nError executing vim.schedule lua callback: Vim:E158: Invalid buffer name: 1349103392\r\nstack traceback:\r\n        [C]: in function 'sign_unplace'\r\n        ...er/.local/share/nvim/lazy/marks.nvim/lua/marks/utils.lua:27: in function 'remove_buf_signs'\r\n        ....local/share/nvim/lazy/marks.nvim/lua/marks/bookmark.lua:297: in function 'refresh'\r\n        ...user/.local/share/nvim/lazy/marks.nvim/lua/marks/init.lua:79: in function ''\r\n        vim/_editor.lua: in function <vim/_editor.lua:0>\r\n```\r\n\r\nnVim crashes.",
