            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nI can not reproduce, mostly because `<C-k>` doesn't open anything for me. If you mean `K` (or `<Shift>`+`k`) for documentation, it opens information in a floating window for me, not a split.\r\n\r\nMoreover, there is no indication that this error comes from 'mini.bufremove'. More likely it is 'marks.nvim' that stumbles after wiped out buffer. Can you reproduce the same error if you execute plain `:bwipeout` (and *not* `:lua MiniBufremove.wipeout()`)?",
