            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Apologies, it is `<S-k>` indeed. Fixed in the original post.\r\n\r\nI have commented-out `marks.nvim` in its entirety, not loaded anymore.\r\n\r\n`:bwipeout` results in this:\r\n```\r\nE315: ml_get: Invalid lnum: 1                                                                                                                                               \r\nError in decoration provider IndentLine.win:\r\nError executing lua: .../share/nvim/lazy/indentmini.nvim/lua/indentmini/init.lua:215: Invalid buffer id: 2                                                                  \r\nstack traceback:                                                                                                                                                            \r\n        [C]: in function '__index'                                                                                                                                          \r\n        .../share/nvim/lazy/indentmini.nvim/lua/indentmini/init.lua:215: in function 'f'                                                                                    \r\n        /usr/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/iter.lua:625: in function 'fn'                                                                                                      \r\n        /usr/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/iter.lua:633: in function 'find'                                                                                                    \r\n        .../share/nvim/lazy/indentmini.nvim/lua/indentmini/init.lua:214: in function <.../share/nvim/lazy/indentmini.nvim/lua/indentmini/init.lua:211>\r\n```\r\n\r\nDocumentation buffer shows the following in the ruler:\r\n```\r\nterm://~/some/path//2856865:ansible-doc ansible.builtin.git\r\n```\r\n\r\nWould you like to see a screencast or a particularly verbose log?\r\n\r\n",
