        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> `:bwipeout` results in this:\r\n\r\nDoes `:lua MiniBufremove.wipeout()` result in the same error?\r\n\r\nMy point is that if `MiniBufremove.wipeout()` and `:bwipeout` result in the same error, then it is not a 'mini.bufremove' issue: [`wipeout()` is a thin wrapper around `:bwipeout`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/998cfcf1fdd0a6830d0fc35f1c054a6f55de1e7f/doc/mini-bufremove.txt#L89). All errors (so far) come from plugins that can not handle the wiped out buffer.",
